Report a top-level parameter block's space in its sub-object range.

ExtendedTypeLayoutContext (source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp) records, for each parameter
group, a sub-object range whose spaceOffset spReflectionTypeLayout_getSubObjectRangeSpaceOffset
returns. A parameter block that starts a space of its own is laid out with
LayoutResourceKind::RegisterSpace, and a nested one with SubElementRegisterSpace, but the range's
spaceOffset is read only for the nested kind. Every top-level parameter block therefore reports
space offset 0: two ParameterBlock globals beside a loose global, which occupy spaces 1 and 2,
both report 0.

This reads the variable's index for whichever of the two kinds the block is laid out with. A
regression test is added as tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-parameter-block-space-offset.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21 (win-x64): 0 and 0 for blocks in spaces 1 and 2.
diff --git a/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp b/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
index 9f83ff5fd..234ece0ea 100644
--- a/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
+++ b/source/slang/slang-reflection-api.cpp
@@ -2238,10 +2238,15 @@ struct ExtendedTypeLayoutContext
             subObjectRange.bindingRangeIndex = bindingRangeIndex;
             subObjectRange.offsetVarLayout = createOffsetVarLayout(typeLayout, path);
             subObjectRange.spaceOffset = 0;
-            if (kind == LayoutResourceKind::SubElementRegisterSpace && path.primary)
+            // A parameter block that starts a space of its own is laid out under `RegisterSpace` (above),
+            // a nested one under `SubElementRegisterSpace`; either way its space is the variable's
+            // index for that kind. Reading only the nested kind reported 0 for every top-level block.
+            //
+            if ((kind == LayoutResourceKind::SubElementRegisterSpace ||
+                 kind == LayoutResourceKind::RegisterSpace) &&
+                path.primary)
             {
-                if (auto resInfo = path.primary->var->FindResourceInfo(
-                        LayoutResourceKind::SubElementRegisterSpace))
+                if (auto resInfo = path.primary->var->FindResourceInfo(kind))
                 {
                     subObjectRange.spaceOffset = resInfo->index;
                 }
